  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Refugee Resettlement Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM is providing comprehensive resettlement support to those refugees identified by the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) and accepted by the Government of Japan (GoJ) for resettlement to Japan. This is in line with the previous project phases (2010-2022), where the Government of Japan has resettled 250 refugees (90 households) to Japan. The project aims to support a durable solution for refugees, including a sustainable integration of the refugees. IOM is facilitating and providing pre-departure assistance, such as pre-migration health activities (PMHA), pre-departure orientation (PDO) and language sessions, facilitating travel document processing, as well as the movement assistance to Japan. This is being conducted in coordination with relevant partners such as the Government of Japan, the Government of Malaysia, and UNHCR. At the destination country in Japan, the project is supporting the integration into new communities in Japan.</narrative>
  </description>
